#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:56 7f70f5531cfd408eb5b0a74873a2668a
msgid "**EnsemblCompara_get_orthologues** (Type: EnsemblComparaTool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:58 5a363792c7e94312b14800f77ed2eace
msgid ""
"Find orthologous genes (genes in different species that evolved from a "
"common ancestor) using Ens..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst e2d0f7c4b75c4ce9b344d189e3f90be2
msgid "EnsemblCompara_get_orthologues tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:64 28c8bd9e55de4755839c126a90c4a1d3
msgid "**Name**: ``EnsemblCompara_get_orthologues``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:66 87600665254e4fada07de069cb3417b1
msgid ""
"**Description**: Find orthologous genes (genes in different species that "
"evolved from a common ancestor) using Ensembl Compara. Essential for "
"comparative genomics - finding the mouse, zebrafish, or fly equivalent of"
" a human gene. Returns orthologue gene IDs, species, homology type (one-"
"to-one, one-to-many), and taxonomy level of divergence. Example: TP53 in "
"human has a one-to-one orthologue (Trp53) in mouse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:70 c11ccb22cf414ff495b66d0e4bf155e7
msgid ""
"``gene`` (string) (required) Gene symbol or Ensembl gene ID. Examples: "
"'BRCA1', 'TP53', 'ENSG00000141510', 'ENSG00000012048'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:73 ae07e7ecb5c04416b8242a23464ca964
msgid ""
"``species`` (string) (optional) Source species (default: 'human'). "
"Examples: 'human', 'mouse', 'zebrafish', 'drosophila\\_melanogaster'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:76 71ee865d1eac4ae18800087922985efd
msgid ""
"``target_species`` (string) (optional) Target species to limit orthologue"
" search. Examples: 'mouse', 'zebrafish', 'rat', "
"'drosophila\\_melanogaster'. Default: all species."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:79 872b097f5be549f9bcbd63370146ed38
msgid ""
"``target_taxon`` (integer) (optional) NCBI taxon ID to limit orthologue "
"search. Examples: 10090 (mouse), 7955 (zebrafish), 7227 (fruit fly). "
"Alternative to target\\_species."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:96 569cd3c153ab431a8f91f2d58c0259cf
msgid "**EnsemblCompara_get_paralogues** (Type: EnsemblComparaTool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:98 6067b02eb6334d6e8b37bc6fd7233f1f
msgid ""
"Find paralogous genes (genes within the same species that arose from gene"
" duplication events) usi..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst 714341edeb554b54a92b12c39de18163
msgid "EnsemblCompara_get_paralogues tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:104 4d1864aab47a4cdb81f961a29d3433b3
msgid "**Name**: ``EnsemblCompara_get_paralogues``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:106 7e41352048794d079289852165aa1bdf
msgid ""
"**Description**: Find paralogous genes (genes within the same species "
"that arose from gene duplication events) using Ensembl Compara. "
"Paralogues often have related but diverged functions. Returns paralogue "
"gene IDs, duplication type, and evolutionary context. Example: TP53 has "
"paralogues TP63 (ENSG00000073282) and TP73 (ENSG00000078900) in human, "
"from ancient vertebrate gene duplication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:110 b8cac8527f3147d5aa7bb4c5b3ef668d
msgid ""
"``gene`` (string) (required) Gene symbol or Ensembl gene ID. Examples: "
"'TP53', 'BRCA1', 'ENSG00000141510'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_compara_tools.rst:113 65699ab0e6c146f28c061d63171e0f93
msgid ""
"``species`` (string) (optional) Species (default: 'human'). Examples: "
"'human', 'mouse', 'zebrafish'."
msgstr ""

